Vesper: refuse a request that changes an object bound read-only, or anything under it,
whatever name reaches it: another letter case, a hard link, a symbolic link, a moved directory.
The server reads the objects from <exports file>.protect and knows them by device and inode
number, not by a mount on one name (TD-073).

